  "solution": {
    "text": "The bond order of carbon-carbon bond is <math> <mrow> <mtext>1</mtext><mtext>.5</mtext></mrow> </math> in benzene.<br />Hence, carbon-carbon bond distance <math> <mrow> <mtext>(1</mtext><mtext>.397</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mover> <mtext>A</mtext> <mtext>o</mtext> </mover> <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow> </math> is less than <math> <mrow> <mtext>C</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>=</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>C</mtext></mrow> </math> single bond <math> <mrow> <mtext>(1</mtext><mtext>.33</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mover> <mtext>A</mtext> <mtext>o</mtext> </mover> <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></mrow> </math> and more than <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> double bond <math> <mrow> <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1.33</mn><mtext> </mtext><mover> <mtext>A</mtext> <mtext>o</mtext> </mover> <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow> </math>",
